{
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "mc_cloze",
      "title": "Đọc điền trắc nghiệm",
      "instructions": "Read the following advertisement and mark the letter A, B, C or D on your answer sheet to indicate the option that best fits each of the numbered blanks from 1 to 6.",
      "passage": "SUMMER PART-TIME JOBS FOR UNDERGRADUATES\n\nTechworld Magazine is delighted to announce two IT assistant vacancies up for (1) ______ this summer. The better understanding of STEM you have, (2) ______ likely you are to be selected! Successful applicants will get plenty of hands-on experience, good pay, and access to the local STEM community.\n\n(3) ______, we offer flexible working hours and remote options for those living far away. On top of that, (4) ______ position requires previous experience as new recruits are provided with in-service training sessions.\n\nApplications (5) ______ be submitted to us at info@techworldmagazine.com by 30 June.\n\nNever before has there been such a(n) (6) ______ opportunity to kick-start your career in STEM. Don’t let this chance slip through your fingers – apply today!",
      "blanks": [
        {
          "question_number": 1,
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "grips" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "gift" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "grasp" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "grabs" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "D",
          "explanation": "Cụm cố định: up for grabs = có sẵn để giành lấy, có thể đăng ký/ứng tuyển.Câu: “two IT assistant vacancies up for grabs” nghĩa là “hai vị trí trợ lý IT đang mở để ứng tuyển”."
        },
        {
          "question_number": 2,
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "most" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "the most" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "the more" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "more" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "C",
          "explanation": "Cấu trúc so sánh kép: The + so sánh hơn ..., the + so sánh hơn ...“The better understanding of STEM you have, the more likely you are to be selected.”Nghĩa: Bạn càng hiểu STEM tốt thì càng có khả năng được chọn."
        },
        {
          "question_number": 3,
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "Additionally" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "Subsequently" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "Consequently" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "Finally" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "A",
          "explanation": "Đoạn trước nói về lợi ích: kinh nghiệm, lương, kết nối cộng đồng STEM. Đoạn sau bổ sung thêm lợi ích: giờ làm linh hoạt, làm từ xa.Additionally = thêm vào đó, ngoài ra. Các đáp án khác: Subsequently = sau đó, về trình tự thời gian. Consequently = do đó, chỉ kết quả. Finally = cuối cùng."
        },
        {
          "question_number": 4,
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "both" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "either" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "none" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "neither" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "D",
          "explanation": "Câu có “position” số ít và nghĩa là “không vị trí nào yêu cầu kinh nghiệm trước đó”.Dùng: neither position requires... = không vị trí nào trong hai vị trí yêu cầu..."
        },
        {
          "question_number": 5,
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "ought not" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "should not" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "ought" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "should" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "D",
          "explanation": "Câu thông báo yêu cầu nộp hồ sơ trước hạn:“Applications should be submitted...” = Hồ sơ nên/cần được nộp...“ought” phải đi với “to”: ought to be submitted, nên đáp án C sai."
        },
        {
          "question_number": 6,
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "lively" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "private" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "active" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "golden" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "D",
          "explanation": "Cụm quen thuộc: a golden opportunity = cơ hội vàng.Câu: “such a golden opportunity to kick-start your career” = một cơ hội vàng để khởi đầu sự nghiệp."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "mc_cloze",
      "title": "Đọc điền trắc nghiệm",
      "instructions": "Read the following passage and mark the letter A, B, C or D on your answer sheet to indicate the option that best fits each of the numbered blanks from 7 to 11.",
      "passage": "Money has many ironies, and here is an important one: wealth is what you do not see. On spotting a Ferrari driving around, (7) ______. In reality, however, many drivers of expensive cars turn out to be only mediocre successes who spend a huge percentage of their paycheck on a vehicle. Someone driving a hundred-thousand-dollar car might indeed be wealthy. Yet the only firm data point you have about their wealth is that they have a hundred thousand dollars less than they did before they bought the car or a hundred thousand dollars more in debt. (8) ______. We tend to judge wealth by what we see (9) ______. We cannot peer into people’s bank accounts or brokerage statements, so we rely on outward appearances to gauge financial success: cars, houses, photographs on social media. Modern capitalism has turned helping people fake it until they make it into a cherished industry. (10) ______. Wealth hides in the nice car not purchased, the diamonds left in the shop and the first-class upgrade declined. Wealth is the financial assets that have not yet been converted into the stuff you see. Hence, we should be careful (11) ______. It is more than mere semantics; not knowing the difference is the source of countless poor money decisions.",
      "blanks": [
        {
          "question_number": 7,
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "you might assume that the owner of the car must be rich" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "you might be assumed to be the rich owner of the car" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "people might assume you must be the rich owner of the car" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "the car might be assumed to be owned by a rich person" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "A",
          "explanation": "Câu trước: “On spotting a Ferrari driving around,...” = Khi nhìn thấy một chiếc Ferrari chạy trên đường...Ý hợp lý: bạn có thể cho rằng chủ xe rất giàu. Các đáp án B, C, D bị lệch chủ thể hoặc diễn đạt bị động không tự nhiên."
        },
        {
          "question_number": 8,
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "All that you know is about them" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "You know what they are all about" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "What you know is about them all" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "That is all you know about them" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "D",
          "explanation": "Trước đó tác giả nói: ta chỉ biết họ có ít hơn 100.000 đô sau khi mua xe hoặc nợ thêm 100.000 đô.Vì vậy câu tiếp theo hợp lý là: That is all you know about them = Đó là tất cả những gì bạn biết về họ."
        },
        {
          "question_number": 9,
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "because external clues are the only information we have to work with" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "rather than by external clues as the only information we have to work with" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "unless we only have external clues as the information to work with" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "other than external clues as the information that we only have to work with" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "A",
          "explanation": "Câu hoàn chỉnh:“We tend to judge wealth by what we see because external clues are the only information we have to work with.”Nghĩa: Ta thường đánh giá sự giàu có bằng thứ ta nhìn thấy vì các dấu hiệu bên ngoài là thông tin duy nhất ta có."
        },
        {
          "question_number": 10,
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "Authentic wealth, as a consequence, secretly exists by remaining truthful" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "Likewise, the truth is that the existence of authentic wealth remains a secret" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "Authentic wealth, similarly, keeps its existence by secretly remaining truthful" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "However, the truth remains that authentic wealth keeps its existence a secret" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "D",
          "explanation": "Đoạn trước nói con người dễ “fake it until they make it”, tức là tạo vẻ ngoài giàu có. Sau đó tác giả chuyển ý: sự giàu có thật sự thường ẩn đi.However phù hợp để chỉ sự đối lập.Câu D diễn đạt đúng ý: sự giàu có thật sự giữ sự tồn tại của nó như một bí mật."
        },
        {
          "question_number": 11,
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "being wealthy and being rich distinguish themselves" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "for being wealthy to be distinguished from being rich" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "being wealthy is distinguishing itself from being rich" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "to distinguish between being wealthy and being rich" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "D",
          "explanation": "Cấu trúc: be careful to do something = cẩn thận khi làm gì.Câu đúng: “we should be careful to distinguish between being wealthy and being rich.”Nghĩa: cần phân biệt giữa “wealthy” và “rich”."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "mc_questions",
      "title": "Trắc nghiệm",
      "instructions": "Mark the letter A, B, C or D on your answer sheet to indicate the best arrangement of utterances or sentences to make a cohesive and coherent exchange or text in each of the following questions from 12 to 16.",
      "variant": "sentence_arrangement",
      "items": [
        {
          "question_number": 12,
          "prompt": "Dear Ms Hoang,\na. A payment of $5,000 will be released in the beginning, and the remaining balance after the submission of your mid-term report.\nb. Failure to respond by the stated date will result in the offer being granted to the next qualified candidate.\nc. We are delighted to inform you that you have been awarded the Young Researcher Grant.\nd. To confirm your acceptance, please sign the attached form and submit it by 31 August.\ne. The funding is intended to support your fieldwork and must not be used for equipment purchases without prior approval.\nYours sincerely,",
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "c – e – a – d – b" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "c – b – e – d – a" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "c – a – b – e – d" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "c – a – b – d – e" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "A",
          "explanation": "Thứ tự hợp lý của thư:\nc. Thông báo được nhận học bổng/tài trợ.\ne. Nêu mục đích sử dụng khoản tài trợ.\na. Nêu cách chi trả tiền.\nd. Hướng dẫn xác nhận chấp nhận tài trợ.\nb. Nêu hậu quả nếu không phản hồi đúng hạn.\nVì vậy thứ tự đúng là c – e – a – d – b."
        },
        {
          "question_number": 13,
          "prompt": "a. Diner: Excuse me, I’ve been waiting so long for my order.\nb. Diner: Thanks for your help.\nc. Waiter: I’m sorry! I’ll check with the kitchen and get back to you immediately.",
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "a – b – c" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "c – b – a" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "a – c – b" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "b – c – a" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "C",
          "explanation": "Đoạn hội thoại hợp lý:\na. Khách phàn nàn đã chờ món quá lâu.\nc. Bồi bàn xin lỗi và nói sẽ kiểm tra với bếp.\nb. Khách cảm ơn.\nThứ tự: a – c – b."
        },
        {
          "question_number": 14,
          "prompt": "a. Customer: What if I don’t keep the original packaging?\nb. Customer: Great. I’ll bring the item and receipt tomorrow.\nc. Customer: I’d like to exchange the electric fan I bought yesterday.\nd. Manager: Sold items can be exchanged within five days, but we don’t give refunds.\ne. Manager: No problem, only your receipt is needed.",
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "c – d – a – e – b" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "a – e – c – d – b" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "a – d – c – e – b" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "c – e – a – d – b" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "A",
          "explanation": "Thứ tự hợp lý:\nc. Khách muốn đổi chiếc quạt đã mua hôm qua.\nd. Quản lý nói hàng có thể đổi trong 5 ngày nhưng không hoàn tiền.\na. Khách hỏi nếu không giữ bao bì gốc thì sao.\ne. Quản lý nói không sao, chỉ cần hóa đơn.\nb. Khách nói sẽ mang hàng và hóa đơn vào ngày mai.\nThứ tự: c – d – a – e – b."
        },
        {
          "question_number": 15,
          "prompt": "a. Initial results were impressive, as villagers reported broadband speeds comparable to city standards with significantly improved reliability.\nb. For years, the isolated villages of central Marsh County struggled with unreliable copper cables that could not handle increasing bandwidth demands.\nc. Consequently, the local council, partnering with two providers, committed to laying fibre optic cables to every household within a year.\nd. To minimise disruption, cables were placed along existing verges, while community halls served as temporary installation hubs.\ne. Encouraged by the villagers’ satisfaction, neighbouring counties have requested guidance on adopting the model for their remote villages.",
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "d – a – e – c – b" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "a – e – d – b – c" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "e – b – a – c – d" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "b – c – d – a – e" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "D",
          "explanation": "Đoạn văn nói về việc cải thiện Internet ở các làng hẻo lánh.\nb. Nêu vấn đề: các làng dùng cáp đồng cũ, mạng yếu.\nc. Hội đồng địa phương quyết định lắp cáp quang.\nd. Cách triển khai để giảm gián đoạn.\na. Kết quả ban đầu rất tốt.\ne. Các hạt lân cận muốn học theo mô hình.\nThứ tự: b – c – d – a – e."
        },
        {
          "question_number": 16,
          "prompt": "a. Inhabitants of coastal regions housing large-scale facilities have reported that the low hum of the constant rotation impairs their sleep quality.\nb. Nevertheless, the argument for transitioning is not entirely convincing when the implications for residents in the immediate vicinity are taken into account.\nc. With the infrastructure in place, operational expenditures of wind mills are substantially lower than those of coal or gas facilities.\nd. Wind power has been promoted as a notably clean and economically viable substitute for fossil fuels.\ne. Progress on a country’s renewable targets necessitates balancing each proposed initiative against the burdens imposed upon local populations.",
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "d – c – b – a – e" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "a – d – c – e – b" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "c – e – d – b – a" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "e – b – a – c – d" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "A",
          "explanation": "Đoạn văn về điện gió.\nd. Giới thiệu điện gió là nguồn thay thế sạch và khả thi.\nc. Nêu ưu điểm chi phí vận hành thấp.\nb. Chuyển ý: tuy nhiên, lập luận chưa hoàn toàn thuyết phục nếu xét đến cư dân gần đó.\na. Nêu vấn đề tiếng ồn ảnh hưởng giấc ngủ cư dân.\ne. Kết luận cần cân bằng mục tiêu năng lượng tái tạo với gánh nặng cho người dân địa phương.\nThứ tự: d – c – b – a – e."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "reading_mixed",
      "title": "Đọc hiểu",
      "instructions": "Read the passage and mark the letter A, B, C or D on your answer sheet to indicate the best answer to each of the following questions from 17 to 24.",
      "passage": "For decades, students have been convinced that academic success is largely dependent upon meticulous notetaking. What has changed in recent years is not the importance of the practice but the tools used to perform it. The keyboard has subtly supplanted the pen, and with it, the nature of how information is recorded during a lecture has shifted unbeknownst to students.\n\nResearchers in cognitive psychology have begun to examine what this change has cost learners. In a series of comparative studies, students taking notes by hand consistently outperformed those using laptops on questions that demanded conceptual understanding, even when both groups had access to the same material. The reason, according to the researchers, lies less in the technology itself than in what each method asks of the brain. Typing rewards speed; handwriting forces selection.\n\nThe act of writing by hand is slower, and that slowness appears to be its hidden virtue. Unable to capture every word, students are obliged to listen, decide what matters and condense ideas into their own phrasing. This continuous filtering, referred to as encoding by psychologists, turns out to be instrumental in aiding long-term recall. One lecturer summarised the striking contrast after reviewing her students’ work: the laptops, she said, had produced transcripts, while the notebooks had produced understanding.\n\nIt would be misleading, of course, to claim that handwriting is inherently superior or that all keyboards undermine learning. Hard-working typists can summarise, while indolent writers can drift. What the research highlights is not a conclusion on devices but a question about effort: which tool, in a given context, asks more of the learner. As a ban on students’ use of laptops in classrooms remains a bone of contention among tertiary institutions, the deeper challenge may be helping students recognise that what feels easier in the moment is not always what serves them best afterwards.\n\n(Adapted from https://www.brookings.edu/)",
      "items": [
        {
          "kind": "mc",
          "question_number": 17,
          "prompt": "In paragraph 1, the writer is ______.",
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "questioning the significance of notetaking in education" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "challenging a long-held assumption about academic success" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "introducing a recent change in the way students take notes" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "promoting the use of technology in recording lectures" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "C",
          "explanation": "Đoạn 1 nói sự thay đổi không nằm ở tầm quan trọng của việc ghi chép mà nằm ở công cụ ghi chép: bàn phím thay thế cây bút.Vì vậy tác giả đang giới thiệu một thay đổi gần đây trong cách học sinh ghi chú."
        },
        {
          "kind": "mc",
          "question_number": 18,
          "prompt": "The word those in paragraph 2 refers to ______.",
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "researchers" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "students" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "notes" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "studies" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "B",
          "explanation": "Câu: “students taking notes by hand consistently outperformed those using laptops...”those ở đây thay cho students.Nghĩa: học sinh ghi chú bằng tay làm tốt hơn những học sinh dùng laptop."
        },
        {
          "kind": "mc",
          "question_number": 19,
          "prompt": "Which of the following best paraphrases the underlined sentence in paragraph 2? The reason, according to the researchers, lies less in the technology itself than in what each method asks of the brain.",
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "What explains the difference in student performance is the mental work that each method of notetaking demands, rather than the technology." },
            { "id": "B", "text": "The modern device, along with the mental requirements of each method for the brain, is responsible for the difference in student performance." },
            { "id": "C", "text": "The difference in student performance is attributable to the modern technology instead of the mental work that each method of notetaking requires." },
            { "id": "D", "text": "Regardless of the method of notetaking, the effects on the brain exhibit little difference as long as technology is involved in student performance." }
          ],
          "correct_id": "A",
          "explanation": "Câu gạch chân nói rằng nguyên nhân nằm ít ở bản thân công nghệ, mà nhiều hơn ở việc mỗi phương pháp yêu cầu bộ não làm gì.Đáp án A diễn đạt đúng nhất: sự khác biệt trong kết quả học tập là do mức độ xử lí tư duy mà mỗi phương pháp ghi chú đòi hỏi, chứ không đơn giản do thiết bị."
        },
        {
          "kind": "mc",
          "question_number": 20,
          "prompt": "The word instrumental in paragraph 3 is OPPOSITE in meaning to ______.",
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "central" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "dramatic" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "specific" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "trivial" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "D",
          "explanation": "instrumental = quan trọng, có vai trò giúp đạt kết quả.Từ trái nghĩa là trivial = không quan trọng, tầm thường."
        },
        {
          "kind": "mc",
          "question_number": 21,
          "prompt": "The word indolent in paragraph 4 is closest in meaning to ______.",
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "active" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "lazy" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "serious" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "careful" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "B",
          "explanation": "indolent = lười biếng.Trong câu: “indolent writers can drift” = người viết tay nhưng lười vẫn có thể mất tập trung."
        },
        {
          "kind": "mc",
          "question_number": 22,
          "prompt": "Which of the following statements would the writer NOT agree with?",
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "Handwritten and typed notes led to varied degrees of conceptual understanding." },
            { "id": "B", "text": "Students are unaware of the change in notetaking methods in class." },
            { "id": "C", "text": "The slow speed of writing by hand turns out to be an advantage over typing." },
            { "id": "D", "text": "Universities generally approve of prohibiting laptop use in classrooms." }
          ],
          "correct_id": "D",
          "explanation": "Câu hỏi hỏi điều tác giả không đồng ý.Đoạn cuối nói việc cấm dùng laptop trong lớp vẫn là “a bone of contention” = vấn đề gây tranh cãi.Vì vậy không thể nói các trường đại học nhìn chung đều ủng hộ việc cấm laptop."
        },
        {
          "kind": "mc",
          "question_number": 23,
          "prompt": "In which paragraph does the writer mention a cognitive process?",
          "options": [
            { "id": "A", "text": "Paragraph 2" },
            { "id": "B", "text": "Paragraph 3" },
            { "id": "C", "text": "Paragraph 1" },
            { "id": "D", "text": "Paragraph 4" }
          ],
          "correct_id": "B",
          "explanation": "Đoạn 3 nhắc đến quá trình nhận thức: encoding = quá trình mã hóa thông tin vào trí nhớ.Vì vậy đáp án là Paragraph 3."
        },
        {
          "kind": "mc",
          "question_number": 24,
          "prompt": "In which paragraph does the writer warn against an overgeneralisation?",
          "options": [
